llp/3000.019-what-the-builder-still-wrote.rfc.md:8:**Revised:** 2026-10-16 (§3.7 SURF3: live-host registry, ambiguity and instance-bound controls); 2026-10-13 (FLAKE: measure actual poll sleep and prove recorder independence); 2026-10-08 (§3.4: `run` forwards through a live dev host, app-farm round 1); 2026-10-04 (AP round 3 docs: exact deadline rewrites versus conditional retirement); 2026-10-04 (AP round 2: surviving-table cleanup advice); 2026-10-04 (AP round 1: refusal order, configurable memory/retry and retirement advice); 2026-10-04 (AP atomic adoption optimization, cost advice and online recommendation); 2026-10-03 (RP round 2: §3.5 device writes retain declared media-list slot charges without ledger custody); 2026-10-03 (§3.3.1: round 3, eviction ordering barriers and viewer retirement across the opening journal read); 2026-10-03 (§3.3.1: round 2, terminal-only retention, admission ordering and outstanding observation retirement); 2026-10-03 (Lane B round 1: bounded mounted ownership, principal/store lifetime, peer settlement and sequence-backed state retirement, §3.3.1); 2026-10-03 (LM committed-mutation trace, §3.7); 2026-10-02 (CT qualification trace and persistent dispatch); 2026-10-02 (RV: narrowed revocation premise, §3.3); 2026-09-29 (LL round 0: dependency-selective retained-media revalidation, §3.5); 2026-09-29 (§3.3 points to the narrowed episode policy in LLP 3000.023 §10); 2026-09-29 (AV round 1: complete ranged downloads retain under the same receipt, §3.5); 2026-09-28 (RG round 6: isolate successful-head recovery and observation-read failures; awaited delivery fault census); 2026-09-28 (RG round 5: housekeeping cannot gate queued dispatch, committed admission or receipt persistence); 2026-09-28 (RG round 4: emission ownership through retirement and outstanding FIFO snapshots); 2026-09-28 (RG round 3: durable terminal notification survives observation and post-commit housekeeping failure); 2026-09-28 (RG round 2: drain unobserved successes at flush exits); 2026-09-28 (RG round 1: sync earlier successes after a refused tail; shared settlement sync and metadata-only media observation); 2026-09-27 (§3.7 SE round 3: synchronous clock maintenance acquisition and CPU attribution); 2026-09-27 (§3.7 SE round 2: distinguish idle CPU distributions from missing clock samples); 2026-09-27 (§3.7 SE round 1: listener fence, independent header attachment and consistent acquisition timing); 2026-09-27 (§3.7: per-response dev timing, cumulative acquisition wait, engine ownership and thread CPU); 2026-09-27 (§3.6: reserve query capacity during atomic Following launch); 2026-09-27 (§3.5: sparse confirmed media markers at scale); 2026-09-27 (§3.4: TK round-1 mutual live-token proofs and confidential replies); 2026-09-27 (§3.3 updated to the implemented LLP 3000.023 contract, KG round 1); 2026-09-27 (§3.3, lane KG: keep the facade-approved answer through replacement authority under its own expiry); 2026-09-27 (§3.3 item 1 revised by LLP 3000.023, Accepted); 2026-09-27 (§3.4: round 2 removes partial sidecar revocation and documents exclusion ending on unlink/replacement); 2026-09-27 (§3.4: reject database aliases and hard links, lock before creation, revoke removed sidecars); 2026-09-27 (§3.5 round 4: request-bound restore proof, staged continuation preflight and open-owner identity adoption); 2026-09-26 (DQ: residency preserves legacy stores until successful adoption); 2026-09-27 (§3.5 round 3: overtaken snapshot continuations retry without a restore halt; receipt-less once regression); 2026-09-27 (§3.5 round 2: paged upgrade restore refusal, store-bound once invalidation and terminal interruption); 2026-09-27 (§3.4: ownership sidecar avoids Darwin SQLite lock conflicts); 2026-09-27 (§3.5 round 1: device-format reacquisition, delayed delivery and stronger home witnesses); 2026-09-27 (§3.5: lane A5 ports list-media offline retention); 2026-09-26 (revision 5, integration: part 2 is a lingering live watch, not a stored answer; P5 shipped as LLP 3000.020 and P7's requirements moved to LLP 3000.021 P13; the lanes table records every 0.4.4 lane; the acceptance measurement is calibration #23); 2026-09-26 (P10 round 2: writer admission, physical key-proof invalidation, production failure cleanup and ephemeral authority); 2026-09-26 (P10 round 1: validation, admission, snapshot evidence, bounded key validation reuse and explicit `/changes` wait); 2026-09-26 (P10: incremental index activation and independent query/sync readers); 2026-09-27 (LT round 3: persisted discovery and explicit loopback URL inspection; held-poll write regression); 2026-09-26 (§3.7 round 2: directory-anchored discovery, server-vouched identity and lifetime, pre-cleanup fallback); 2026-09-26 (§3.7 round 1: flush-bound completion, per-operation snapshots, independent dev discovery); 2026-09-26 (§3.7: lane LT implements server operation latency); 2026-09-26 (lane EK: the ephemeral card opts its typing reads into `keep`, with expiry still fenced); 2026-09-26 (§6: the author's hold for the image-list placement fix); 2026-09-26 (revision 4: keeping answers is an opt-in `keep`, after lane K showed the platform cannot tell a revoking commit); 2026-09-26 (revision 3: P3's retention narrowed by authority, after lane K found revocation arrives by ordinary commits); 2026-09-26 (revision 2: P4 answered by LLP 3000.015's row-keyed views, shipping in 0.4.3; P5 narrowed to expiry on the device); 2026-09-26 (revision 1: concrete designs for P1, P2, P3 and P8; P4, P5 and P7 scoped as their own RFCs; lanes and acceptance); 2026-09-26 (initial)
