snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/deploy.md:118:`data TABLE --release ./deployment --json` returns `{rows, more, limit}`. The default limit is 50; `more:true` means the snapshot was truncated. Increase `--limit N` to inspect more; `--limit 0` returns no rows and reports whether any exist. Non-JSON output remains one row per line.
snapback4/crates/snapback4-lang/src/guide/deploy.md:137:`deploy --check --json` reports `clientCompatibility` separately from data adoption: missing operations, changed kinds, required new arguments, removed or narrowed inputs, result shape/value changes and changed refusal codes/messages. Deploy prints the same warnings. Input breaks name the old release and the E_INPUT/E_OP outcome. A result or behavior review asks you to verify the intended contract; a correct new privacy denial is intentional behavior, not an input shape failure. The comparison is conservative, not a proof of unchanged logic. For example, save this v1 source and its callers sending `{name:"Ada",obsolete:"old input"}` to `greet`:
